    "Notes Updated": "5/21/2022",
    "Scouting Notes": "New arm action post surgery (Thoracic Outlet).\n Similar to adjustment Eric Lauer has made since coming to Milwaukee, shorter arm action.\n Kelly seems much more comfortable with this change in 2022 vs 2021.\n Fastball velocity isn't quite where it was pre draft, but command of it is improved.\n Slider was seen as a mediocre secondary pre draft. I'd say it borders on a plus pitch now.\n Changeup developing, but nothing too exciting yet.\n Huge strikeout numbers, walks have been cut a bit.\n With Ashby graduated, this is my current top pitching prospect in the org (surpassed when Misiorowski was drafted)\n High ceiling, floor has raised slightly since surgery. Still a lot of reliever risk in the profile. Likely needs improved 3rd pitch to stick in rotation.\n If 3rd pitch develops, I can see a mid rotation arm. If not, likely pen arm with chance to be high leverage.",
